 {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-5", "title": "Data-quality footnote is fleet-global in serve: multi-board reports list another board's no-done ids in every report, including single-board ones", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-09-20 (dogfood run, serve surface).\nEVIDENCE: the 3-board serve upload of [boardctl, b2] has payload.completed_no_done_ids = [CHT-007, CHT-008, CHT-023, CHT-026, CHT-027, CHT-046, CHT-050] - those are coding-hermes-tools (b2) row ids. The render footer reads payload.completed_no_done_ids and prints 'completed tasks with no computable completion day (never counted in time series): <ids>' under a 'Data quality' heading (template.go:1321-1324) - it is NOT scoped per board, so a viewer looking at the boardctl board inside that report is shown b2's uncomputable rows as if they were boardctl's. Confirmed the mechanism in code: report.go BuildBoards:80-94 unions noDoneCompletedIDs(d) across ALL boards into one payload-level set, while every other per-board field is namespaced under boards[]. Contrast with single-board render, where the payload-level field happens to be correct because there is only one board.\nIMPACT: an attribution defect in the exact place the report is meant to build trust - the honesty footnote names the wrong board on every multi-board (serve) report, which is the report's flagship mode. On a large fleet upload it degenerates into an unattributable id dump.\nFIX DIRECTION: move completed_no_done_ids under each boards[] entry (or key the payload-level set by board slug/name) and render it in that board's own panel.", "created_at": "2026-09-20T04:49:37Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-20T05:36:45Z", "worker_status": "pending", "detail": {"fingerprint": "bb871826ed9e35d15c90f986e1e7f1edbb25c1e0fc7a384f8bc833bb92cbc198"}, "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "foreman_note": "wave dispatch tick boardctl-2026-09-20-04-54-08", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/coding-hermes-boardctl-DF-BOARDCTL-5", "branch": "wt/DF-BOARDCTL-5